            "snippet": "Lifespan:",
            "list": [
              {
                "snippet": "Asphalt shingles: Lasts about 20 to 30 years."
              },
              {
                "snippet": "Metal roof: Lasts about 40 to 75+ years (often 2 to 3 times longer).",
                "reference_indexes": [
                  2,
                  4,
                  8
                ]
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              4,
              8
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Upfront vs. Long-Term Value: While metal costs roughly 1.7 to 3 times more initially, it frequently outlasts two full cycles of asphalt shingle replacements in Utah's heavy snow, freeze-thaw, and intense summer sun cycles.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Weather & Maintenance: Metal sheds heavy mountain snow and ice quickly and is fire-resistant, whereas asphalt is more budget-friendly initially. You can explore local insights via The Provo Roof Pros Blog .",
